Library Modules – Dog Activity Tracker
This folder contains modular components for each milestone of the Dog Activity Tracker firmware. Each module encapsulates specific functionality required to simulate, classify, and log dog activities on the ESP32-CAM.

⚪Milestone 1.1 – Simulated Accelerometer
Simulates the QMI8658 sensor behavior using random motion data. Includes a callback mechanism to trigger actions when motion is "detected."

Files:
SimulatedQMI8658/SimulatedQMI8658.h
SimulatedQMI8658/SimulatedQMI8658.cpp
MotionManager/MotionManager.h
MotionManager/MotionManager.cpp

⚪Milestone 1.2 – Sleep Management
Implements deep sleep on the ESP32 and tracks how many times the board has woken up using RTC memory. Also includes a periodic 2-minute wake timer to simulate wake-on-time behavior.

Files:
SleepManager/SleepManager.h
SleepManager/SleepManager.cpp
WakeupTimer/WakeupTimer.h
WakeupTimer/WakeupTimer.cpp

⚪Milestone 1.3 – Time Synchronization
Handles real-time clock (RTC) operations and synchronizes system time with NTP servers when Wi-Fi is available. Displays current and last sync time.

Files:
TimeManager/TimeManager.h
TimeManager/TimeManager.cpp

⚪Milestone 1.4 – Activity Classification
Takes simulated IMU data and classifies the current activity into one of four states: Resting, Walking, Running, or Playing based on magnitude thresholds.

Files:
ActivityClassifier/ActivityClassifier.h
ActivityClassifier/ActivityClassifier.cpp

⚪Milestone 1.5 – Data Logging
Tracks the time spent in each activity state and logs this data every 10 minutes into a LittleFS file with a timestamp. Generates daily logs in binary format.

Files:
ActivityLogger/ActivityLogger.h
ActivityLogger/ActivityLogger.cpp
